    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d949">

                <pb facs="0734" n="618" xml:id="pg618"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/13704.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Special Agent Canova to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Aguascalientes</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-05T23:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 5, 1914, 11 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Convention to-day received telegram from Carranza insisting on his
                    conditions, and telegram from Obregón asking for an extension of time for
                    Carranza so as to date the twenty days of Gutiérrez as Provisional President
                    from his assumption of office. It was decided to send Carranza. telegraphic
                    ultimatum that he deliver the Executive Power to Gutiérrez by November 10, 6
                    p.m. General Gutiérrez will take the oath of office to-morrow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canova</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
